  "details": "This is a problem that arises when multiple people are developing a single project using Git.\n\nWhen you add an existing project that has been loaded using Git or something like that, depending on the individual's environment, packages that are not linked to VCC will not be included in the project.\n\nIt is difficult to make everyone's environment the same, such as linking community packages to VCC and matching the versions of each package.\n\nSo, as shown in this image, I would like you to create a screen that links the repository of the missing package to VCC, and a screen that adds the packages in the linked repository to the project.\n\nIt is also fine to remove the screen in Image No. 4 and automatically add the packages.",
